					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: CREATING A BOUNDING BOX FOR A SHAPE\n\nIn this example we have a Star shape that is randomly moving around the screen.\nThe random movement is generated by the two Perlin Generator nodes.\nWe created the \"bounding box\" by creating a Rectangle geometry and converting it to a Box2D by using the Bounding Box node.\nNext, we check if the Float2 generated by the two Perlin Generator nodes (the position of the Star), is Within the box.\nIf so, we switch to rendering with a red color.\n\nCombining To Box with Within\/Outside is very useful as it allows you to check whether a Float2 value is within\/outside the bounds of a Box2D type."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 741.39013671875,
					"width": 1503.8641357421875,
					"x": 246.2837371826171875,
					"y": 86.62005615234375
				},
